---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";
import { visitIdsForArticle } from "../../data/catalog";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "guides")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics Guides"
  description="Analytics guides on marketing attribution tools, cookieless analytics, and the DataFast API and MCP. Each guide says who should act and what the choice costs."
  kicker="Guides"
  lede="These guides explain a decision, then compare the tools that can carry it. They are not one ranked list of logos."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Guides" }]}
>
  <p>Marketing attribution asks which visit should get credit for a payment. Cookieless analytics asks how stable that credit can be without a long-lived browser identifier. Those guides stay separate, because a cookieless script and a long revenue journey pull in opposite directions once a sale takes weeks.</p>
  <p>Two DataFast guides sit next to those decisions. The <a href="/guides/datafast-api/">DataFast API</a> page covers website keys, goal events, revenue, and the CLI. The <a href="/guides/datafast-mcp/">DataFast MCP</a> guide is the assistant connection for an account you already have. Neither one is a pricing page or a review. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a>, the <a href="/pricing/datafast/">DataFast pricing</a> ladder, the <a href="/alternatives/datafast/">DataFast alternatives</a>, and the <a href="/compare/datafast-vs-plausible/">DataFast vs Plausible</a> comparison are the neighboring pages. Details are as of 26 November 2026.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Analytics guides</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
          visits: visitIdsForArticle(article.id),
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
